    "mythic_text_raw": null,
    "source_book_raw": null,
    "source_page_raw": null,
    "supplemental_sources_raw": [],
    "pfs_status_raw": null,
    "sections_raw": [
      {
        "heading_raw": null,
        "body_raw": "This spell makes the duration of certain other spells permanent. You first cast the desired spell and then follow it with the permanency spell.\n\nDepending on the spell, you must be of a minimum caster level and must expend a specific gp value of diamond dust as a material component.\n\nYou can make the following spells permanent in regard to yourself.\n\nYou cannot cast these spells on other creatures. This application of permanency can be dispelled only by a caster of higher level than you were when you cast the spell.\n\nIn addition to personal use, permanency can be used to make the following spells permanent on yourself, another creature, or an object (as appropriate).\n\nAdditionally, the following spells can be cast upon objects or areas only and rendered permanent.\n\nSpells cast on other targets are vulnerable to dispel magic as normal. The GM may allow other spells to be made permanent."
      }
    ]
  },
